mm/memcontrol: drop uninitialized_var() (removed from grafted 5.10 headers)

The macro uninitialized_var() was removed upstream (v5.10); the e404 base
grafts 5.10-era compiler headers, so it is undefined. MEMCG was previously
disabled so memcontrol.c never compiled; enabling MEMCG exposed this. Plain
declaration is fine with modern Clang 20.

Signed-off-by: Otavio Henrique Franco de Morais <otavio.hfmorais@sp.senac.br>

diff --git a/mm/memcontrol.c b/mm/memcontrol.c
--- a/mm/memcontrol.c
+++ b/mm/memcontrol.c
@@ -919,7 +919,7 @@
 				   struct mem_cgroup *prev,
 				   struct mem_cgroup_reclaim_cookie *reclaim)
 {
-	struct mem_cgroup_reclaim_iter *uninitialized_var(iter);
+	struct mem_cgroup_reclaim_iter *iter;
 	struct cgroup_subsys_state *css = NULL;
 	struct mem_cgroup *memcg = NULL;
 	struct mem_cgroup *pos = NULL;